      "judgment": {
        "status": "source_error",
        "reasoning": "All four final diagrams are mathematically correct and agree with the captured MA answers. q-184489 consists of exactly four points: (-1,-3), (-1,1), (2,-3), and (2,1). q-181306 consists of two closed horizontal segments at y=-1 and y=1, with -1≤x≤1. q-181959 consists of lattice points with positive integer x and arbitrary integer y, using MA's evidenced convention that natural numbers start at 1. Its worked solution contains an authored error: the prose describing S₂ says y is a natural number, whereas its formula and diagram correctly include all integers. q-181968 consists of lattice points with negative integer x and positive integer y. The batch is marked source_error for the q-181959 explanatory error; none of the final answer selections disagree with MA.",
